## Context

Reading-1 item 14 said "Em-dashes are an AI tell — sweep and restyle."
The manuscript body carries ~187 em dashes (as `---`, converted to
Unicode — by ticket 0558/PR #1017). Author decision (2026-06-12): em
dashes stay legal — the tell is *clustering and monotony*, not the
character. Therefore: an editorial once-over that diversifies the
punctuation, plus standing tests that cap density and prevent
regression.

## Actions

1. Once-over editorial pass on `slides/manuscript/main.tex` body prose:
   where em dashes cluster, diversify — commas, colons, parentheses,
   sentence splits. Editor's heuristic (guidance, NOT a test): avoid
   em dashes in consecutive paragraphs; prefer at most one per
   paragraph unless it is a paired parenthetical `—like this—`.
   Exclusions: verbatim/quoted material (the as-sent Doc-07 prompt
   block is frozen), table/figure syntax, the Glossary box quotes.
2. Standing adherence tests (extend
   `tests/test_manuscript_cohort_and_caveats.py` or a new
   test_manuscript_emdash.py):
   a. **Local cap (hard):** no body-prose paragraph (blank-line-
      delimited block, excluding verbatim/quote environments and
      comments) contains more than 2 em dashes.
   b. **Global ratchet (hard):** total body-prose em-dash count ≤ a
      committed ceiling stored in a one-line data file the test reads
      (e.g. tests/data/emdash_ceiling.txt). Lowering the ceiling is a
      deliberate commit; any edit pushing the count above it fails CI.
      Initialize the ceiling to the post-once-over count.
3. Existing abstract guard semantics unchanged.

## Test

- Red first: the paragraph-cap test against pre-once-over main.tex
  (expected to fail on current clusters), and the ratchet test with
  the ceiling file absent/lower than the count.

## Verification

- [ ] Once-over diff is punctuation-only (no semantic rewording);
      author spot-reads at next reading
- [ ] `make -C slides manuscript` builds; PDF renders correctly
- [ ] Both tests pass at the post-sweep count; ceiling committed

## Invariants

- Doc-07 verbatim block byte-identical (drift guard green)
- `make check` green; crossref and macro adherence suites untouched

## Exit criteria

- [x] Author decision recorded in this log (2026-06-12: diversify +
      ratchet, no ban)
- [ ] Once-over executed; em-dash usage diversified
- [ ] Local cap (≤2/paragraph) + global ratchet tests standing
- [ ] `make check` green
